Planned, not in this build. Running one of these verbs exits 2 with the
same line as below.

  record   Record a channel or the raw capture to a file (Milestone C.12)
           today: ley play <file> plays back an IQ recording; recording is a daemon job and is not in this build
  watch    Watch a frequency and log what is heard (Milestone D.15)
           today: ley tune <freq> listens live; keeping a log of what is heard is a daemon job and is not in this build

Decoding is in this build: 'ley decoders' lists the plugins, 'ley decode'
runs one, 'ley records' searches what kept jobs wrote and 'ley track' draws
the live table. Still to come there: predicates and notifications, 'ley
label' and 'ley devices-seen', and 'ley identify'.

The daemon-side relative squelch (mute at 'noise floor + N dB' measured by
the daemon rather than by ley) is the recorded follow-up to auto squelch.
